		(uuid "6e3fe80a-19f0-581e-ad30-2dce23d14549")
	)
	(text "POWER\n  USB-C (5 V, Rd sink) -> BQ24074 charger/power path -> VSYS (4.4 V on USB, VBAT on battery)\n  1S Li-ion 3.7 V 4000 mAh on J103 (JST-PH, pin 1 = +) behind DW01A + FS8205A protection\n  Charge 1.0 A (R104 887R), input limit 1.42 A (R105 1.13k), safety timer ~9 h (R106 68k)\n  PWR switch SW101 -> P-FET Q102 -> VSYS_SW -> TPS63001 3.3 V (always on) + TPS61023 5 V (BOOST_EN)\n  Charging and the fuel gauge keep working with the switch OFF.\n\nMCU <-> CHARGER / GAUGE\n  MAX17048 fuel gauge  I2C 0x36 on PM bus: SDA GPIO0, SCL GPIO5 (FC0), ~ALRT -> GPIO57\n  BQ24074 ~CHG -> GPIO55 (low = charging, high = done/idle), ~PGOOD -> GPIO56 (low = USB present)\n\nRW612 PIN MAP (same as FRDM-RW612 where applicable)\n  LCD (LCDIC SPI)  SCK 48, MOSI 46, DC 47, CS 49, RST 44, backlight PWM 1 (CT0_MAT1)\n  Touch FT6336U    I2C SDA 16/SCL 17 (0x38), INT 18, RST 19      NeoPixel DIN   9 (FC1 SPI MOSI) via 74AHCT1G125\n  EC11 #1          A 2, B 3, SW 4                        EC11 #2        A 50, B 51, SW 52\n  Buttons          BTN1 11, BTN2 25                      User LED       12 (active low)\n  Console UART     TX 26, RX 24 (FC3)                    SWD            SWCLK 13, SWDIO 14, RESET = PDn\n  QSPI flash       28-34 (W25Q512JV)                     PSRAM          35-41 (APS6404L)\n  32 kHz crystal   22/23                                 5 V enable     58   Expansion PM I2C + 20, 21\n\nNOTES\n  * Firmware must drive BOOST_EN (GPIO58) high to power the LCD and NeoPixels (pull-down keeps 5 V off at reset).\n  * Keep BOOST_EN high while the LCD/touch lines are driven (unpowered LCD would be back-fed).\n  * LCD SD-card pins (SD_CS, MISO) are intentionally not connected.\n  * RF: FRDM-RW612 front end (5 GHz pi filter, 2.4 GHz / BLE switch, diplexer) to U.FL J401.\n  * Footprints for RW612 BGA, SKY13323 and the TDK diplexer are project footprints - verify against vendor drawings.\n  * This schematic is generated by steering_wheel.py (SKiDL). Edit the script and re-run instead of editing sheets."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
